  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2021-01-04T23:08:01.309Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Vive's analog input, aka \"Normalized Time\" of the parameters \"GestureLeftWeight\" and \"GestureRightWeight\", only seems to work with VRChat's built-in \"proxy_\" animations and not when a custom one is applied.\n1. Use the example HandLayer controller supplied by the SDK and put it in the gesture layer.\n2. Enter the controller and replace the proxy animation on a state with a custom one on the desired gesture.\n3. Upload avatar and see there is no analog input.\nNotes: The same issue occurs if you simply rename a proxy animation to a custom name, as it's no longer using the built-in proxy animation.",
